---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const { owner, country, lastUpdated } = site.legal;
const formService = site.demo.formEndpoint;
---
<TextPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  path="/privacy/"
  updated={lastUpdated}
  description={`How ${site.name} handles your information: no tracking, no ads, no analytics. What happens when you play a song, send a demo or email us.`}
>
  <p class="note">
    <strong>In short:</strong> {site.url.replace('https://', '')} has no accounts, no analytics, no advertising and sets no
    tracking cookies. Fonts and images are served from this site. Videos load from YouTube only when you press play.
    If you email us, we use your message to reply.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This website is run by {owner} ("we", "us"). For anything about your information, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you browse</h3>
  <p>
    We do not collect personal information when you browse this site. We do not use analytics tools, advertising
    networks, tracking pixels or fingerprinting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Like every website, the services that deliver it see technical data needed to send you the page, such as your IP
    address, browser type and the time of the request. This website is hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub,
    Inc.) and its domain uses <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc.) for DNS and may use it for security and
    caching. These providers may keep short-lived logs for security and to keep the service running. We do not receive or
    use these logs. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>
    and the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>When you play a song or video</h3>
  <p>
    Songs and videos on this site are YouTube videos. Nothing from YouTube loads until you press play. When you do, the
    video player loads from <strong>youtube-nocookie.com</strong> (YouTube's privacy-enhanced mode, operated by Google).
    From that point, YouTube may store information on your device and collect data such as your IP address and what you
    watch, under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    Audio previews hosted on this site, if any, play without contacting third parties.
  </p>

  <h3>When you contact us or send a demo</h3>
  {formService ? (
    <p>
      The demo form sends what you type (name, email, artist name, city, link and message) to our form service, which
      forwards it to us by email. We use it only to listen to your music and reply.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      The demo form does not send anything to us by itself. It opens your own email app with the details you typed, and
      nothing is sent until you press send there. When you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you
      write, and we use it only to listen to your music, answer you, and arrange bookings, press or orders.
    </p>
  )}
  <p>We keep emails for as long as we need them for that conversation, and delete them if you ask.</p>

  <h3>Stored on your device</h3>
  <p>
    The music player remembers your volume level in your browser's local storage (<code>baaz-volume</code>). It never
    leaves your device and you can clear it in your browser settings at any time. We set no cookies.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell, rent or trade personal information.</li>
    <li>We do not use your information for advertising or profiling.</li>
    <li>We do not share your messages with anyone, except when the law requires it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to YouTube, streaming services and social networks. Those sites have their own privacy policies,
    which apply once you open them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us to tell you what information we hold about you, correct it, or delete it, and you can withdraw any
    consent you gave. This applies to everyone, including under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 and,
    for visitors in the EU or UK, the GDPR. Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will reply
    within 30 days. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to your local data protection authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is for a general audience. If you are under 18, please ask a parent or guardian before emailing us or
    sending a demo.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served only over HTTPS and uses a strict Content Security Policy. If you find a security problem, please
    tell us at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> (see also <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a>).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we change how we handle information, we will update this page and the date at the top. This policy is governed by
    the laws of {country}.
  </p>
</TextPage>
